1. An atomic force microscope apparatus, comprising:

a metrology frame;

a sample support coupled to the metrology frame and configured to support a sample having a nanostructure;

a sensor head coupled to the metrology frame, the sensor head including a cantilever probe having a probe tip configured to interact with a surface of the sample;

an actuator scanning mechanism configured to produce relative scanning motion between the probe tip and the sample support in at least one scanning direction;

wherein the probe tip is a fixed-offset angled probe tip having a tip axis inclined relative to a longitudinal axis of the cantilever and laterally offset from the cantilever, the fixed-offset angled probe tip being configured to access and measure a steep sidewall of the nanostructure; and

a three-point kinematic mounting interface configured to removably and repeatably locate at least one of the sensor head, the sample support, or a probe-carrying module relative to the metrology frame.

1. A scanning probe microscope for sensing high aspect ratio features of a sample, the high aspect ratio features having sidewall slopes above a threshold angle, the scanning probe microscope comprising:

a sample support configured to support the sample;

a probe comprising a cantilever and a sensing tip;

an actuator arrangement configured to produce relative scanning movement between the sample support and the probe in at least one lateral direction and to control a spacing between the sample and the probe in a height direction;

wherein the sensing tip is an angled tip having a longitudinal sensing portion inclined relative to the height direction so as to access and sense a sidewall of one of the high aspect ratio features having a slope above the threshold angle; and

a sensor head comprising the probe and being mounted to the scanning probe microscope by a detachable sensor head carrier,

characterised in that the detachable sensor head carrier is removably coupled to a receiving structure of the scanning probe microscope by at least three mutually spaced contact points defining a reproducible kinematic mounting position of the sensor head relative to the sample support.
